&lt;p dir="ltr" style="margin-left:0.8910064697265625pt; text-align:center"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:12px"&gt;###&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Two Defendants Indicted for Forced Labor, Victim Tampering, Aggravated Identity Theft, Mail Fraud, and Wire Fraud involving &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Yakima and Benton County H-2A Workers and&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Four Defendants Charged via Superseding Indictment for Fraud and Exploitation-Related Federal Offenses involving Yakima and Benton County H-2A Workers&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Clarkston, WA --&amp;nbsp;Students and faculty at Clarkston High School are hard at work preparing exciting opportunities for students to explore potential career paths over the course of the month of February, which is nationally recognized as Career and Technical Education (CTE) Month.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;On Friday, February 20th,&lt;strong&gt; 68 &lt;/strong&gt;students from Clarkston High School&rsquo;s Career and Technical Education (CTE) programs had the opportunity to visit local businesses in our area to connect their classroom learning to real-world scenarios. Students learned about careers in a variety of fields, from manufacturing and aviation to marketing and restaurant management.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Clarkston High School would like to thank the following businesses for opening their doors to the next generation of our community&rsquo;s workforce:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
     &lt;li&gt;Lewiston Airport&lt;/li&gt;
     &lt;li&gt;CCI Speer&lt;/li&gt;
     &lt;li&gt;Brava&rsquo;s and Brock&rsquo;s&lt;/li&gt;
     &lt;li&gt;Pat&rsquo;s Garden Center&lt;/li&gt;
     &lt;li&gt;TriState Health&lt;/li&gt;
     &lt;li&gt;Custom Weld and Riverview Marina&lt;/li&gt;
     &lt;li&gt;Schweitzer Engineering Labs (SEL)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
On Tuesday, February 24th, Clarkston High School will host &ldquo;Clarkston Career Conne&lt;strong&gt;CTE&lt;/strong&gt;d,&rdquo; an event inviting community members, local business leaders, and parents to explore the various programs and course offerings available to students at Clarkston High School. The event will be held from 5:00 p.m. to 7:00 p.m. in the Adams building at CHS.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
###&lt;/p&gt;

